WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.390
So with the new IT movie coming out in just
a couple day, I figured I better do that video

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.490
I promised where I answer your IT questions.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.530
Cynder is out of town right now, so it's just
gonna be me answering the questions, but I'm

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.220
feeling pretty confident that I can give you
guys a satisfying answer.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.590
The first question comes from Chloe Froud.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.730
She asks, "Do you think IT will take the shape
of the other forms that weren't shown in the

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.609
mini series such as Jaws?"

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:28.800
That's a good question Chloe.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.480
Yes, I do think that we'll see it take other
forms, but I'm not so sure about Jaws.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.079
I talked about this a little bit in my Ideas
for IT at Halloween Horror Nights, check that

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:42.329
video out here if you haven't seen it, and
basically what I said is that in the book

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:47.110
and the miniseries which take place in the
50s, IT takes the form of some of the movie

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.000
monsters from back then: the most notable
one being Richie having an encounter with

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.739
the Wolfman after going to see The Wolfman
film in theaters and being afraid of it because

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.410
it is constantly praying on the fears of its
victims so my idea was that instead of using

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:06.110
classic 50's horror icons is that this movie
would you use classic 80s for icons like Freddy,

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.270
Jason, Chucky and Michael Myers.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:13.540
So to answer the part of your question about
Jaws, I doubt that we'll see Jaws in this

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.571
movie, because that movie came out in 1975,
so it'd be more applicable to if this what

00:01:18.571 --> 00:01:21.500
movie was taking place in the 70s as opposed
to the 80s.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.150
Yes, it was still relevant in the 80s, but
I just don't see a spot for Jaws to really

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.659
appear in Derry.

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:32.509
The only major body of water is the Kenduskeag
stream, and I think it would be a little bit

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.320
silly for a shark to appear out of a stream.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.820
It could happen but I think it's more likely
that we'll see horror icons from the 80s in

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.820
this film.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.850
Next question comes from Angelo Zarola.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:46.829
"Are all of Pennywise's red balloons the dead
children that he's eaten?"

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:52.009
Well, if you look at it in a literal sense,
no, there is a separate physical manifestation

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:56.400
of the dead children which appears at the
end of the story, which I'm not going to spoil

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.960
right now, for those who haven't seen the
movie.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.400
But in a more symbolic sense, I would say
yes, they do represent the dead children,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:07.460
which is why Pennywise is always using the
line, "you'll float too," or "you'll float

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.780
down here," because each of Pennywise's victims
does float, again I don't want to give it

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:16.630
away, and I think the red balloons are kind
of a physical manifestation of that in the

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.630
real world.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.650
So yes, the balloons do kind of represent
his victims.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:25.290
Gavin K asks our next question, "will the
IT movie be in two parts?"

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.430
Yes, it will.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:31.069
So the movie was originally supposed to come
out as IT: Part 1 - The Loser's Club, and

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:33.870
then at some point they simplified the title
to just "IT".

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:38.200
But it is still going to be a 2-parter like
the miniseries was with the child portion

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.480
taking place first and the adult portion taking
place in Part 2.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.700
I think that the main difference between this
movie and the mini-series, is that in the

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.530
mini-series it kind of sticks to the formula
laid out by the book, where it actually starts

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.460
with the Lucky 7 as adults being called back
to their home town to face IT again based

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.660
on the promise that they made years ago.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.600
As each one of them is called back, they remember
what happened to them in Derry, and they have

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.340
these flashbacks to their encounters with
Pennywise as children.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.430
So it has kind of a nonlinear story structure,
where it takes place in the present but it

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:13.680
has these flashbacks to their childhood memories
in the past and we see how things unfolded.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.769
My prediction is that this new movie is not
going to do that and it's just gonna tell

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:20.989
the story in a linear fashion with the beginning
starting at the very beginning of the child

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:24.909
portion and Part 1 stretching until that promise
is made.

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:28.840
And then Part 2 will just include their lives
as adults and not include those flashbacks

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:29.910
to their childhood.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.409
Matty Plays asks, "doesn't IT live in the
sewers?", and that's a response to the video

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:40.080
that I did showing the IT Neibolt House and
the hashtag #thatswhereitlives basically implying

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.220
that IT lives in 29 Neibolt.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.549
In the book, yes, it does live in the sewers.

00:03:44.549 --> 00:03:49.190
I think the best way for me to explain this
is that the 29 Neibolt House is like IT's

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:53.879
HQ up on the surface, whereas it's true home
is down in the sewers.

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:58.239
We also see in the trailer and the IT experience
itself, which if you want to check out that

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:03.290
video, here is the link, that 29 Neibolt seems
to be connected to the sewers and there's

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.540
a scene where they use a projector to line
up the map of the sewers to the map of Derry

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.360
and basically show that the sewer lines run
right under the 29 Neibolt House.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.120
There's a scene in the book where they actually
venture into 29 Neibolt and confront Pennywise

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.829
and Pennywise actually retreats from there
down into the sewers, where they eventually

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:23.130
go to have their final confrontation with
him.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.030
So I would expect something similar here.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.150
Neazyy Squad asks, "Do you think that this
movie will be better than the TV series??

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.620
Or will it be bad and horrible?"

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.960
Him of course referring to the 1990 TV mini-series
starring Tim Curry.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.650
I have high hopes for this movie.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.080
I think with each trailer that's come out
I've gotten more excited for it.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.550
I've talked to a couple people who have seen
the film and heard nothing but positive things

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:44.550
so far.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.740
So I'm not really expecting a disappointment.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.830
Do I think it will be better than the TV mini-series?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.889
Well, I think there's definitely a chance
for it to be.

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:54.610
The mini-series, in my opinion, is very good.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:58.740
I think this movie is going to do a lot of
things that the mini-series just was not able

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.740
to.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.610
I've talked about this a little bit in Things
You Missed, but one example is the inclusion

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.110
of Patrick Hockstetter, who I'll just say
is a character who does some extremely dark

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.030
things in the book that couldn't be included
in the mini-series.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:13.580
And I've heard that this new movie will just
go to those darker places; go to those more

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.610
extreme lengths.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:18.810
And this is one of many examples in the book
of just how dysfunctional this town of Derry

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:19.810
is.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.370
How all of the adults seem to be willing to
turn a blind eye to the horrible things that

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:27.460
are happening to these kids, and I hope that
we can see more of that in this new movie.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.700
Now, will it live up to what we were given
with the mini-series?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:35.210
Again, I think it will be different, but I'm
hoping with the increased budget and R-rating,

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.900
that it will live up to what we were given
in 1990 and maybe even surpass it.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.240
And another thing is that Part 2 will be very
interesting because the best part of the mini-series

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.590
is the child portion.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.240
And there're still a lot of things that I
like about the adult portion, the very ending

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.810
not being one of them.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.800
But if you ask pretty much anyone what their
favorite part was, they're probably going

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:58.270
to say Part 1, so what I'm most interested
to see is how Part 2 is going to compare to

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.880
Part 2 of the mini-series.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.979
I'm hoping that they might take it in a different
direction and hopefully include the thing

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:08.490
that happens after the ending of the mini-series
that happens in the book.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.240
If you guys have read the book you know what
I'm talking about.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.699
OK, next we're gonna get into some spoiler
questions so if you haven't read the book,

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:19.620
I recommend clicking away or pausing this
video and reading the book...

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.569
It's a long book.

00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:26.750
Mineblox20 says, "I think they'll have a spot
where they show "IT" as the spider creature.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.750
What do you think?

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.460
Well, I think it's pretty unlikely that we'll
see that in this film.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:33.930
I think if they do decide to go with the spider
again that it will be in Part 2.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.569
So, do I think that it will be in Part 2?

00:06:36.569 --> 00:06:40.949
Yes, I think that we'll see it, but I think
they may shift away from that being like the

00:06:40.949 --> 00:06:42.510
final boss kind of thing.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.440
It's something that works a little bit better
on paper, but I think it's just more fitting

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:49.910
for the clown that terrorized them through
the entire thing to be the final boss as opposed

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.069
to this spider which kind of comes out of
nowhere.

00:06:53.069 --> 00:06:57.710
I do understand the reasoning for the spider,
because the Lucky 7, or what's left of them,

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:02.500
come together and IT is unable to find something
that they're all afraid of, and this is really

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.350
like the best form that it can manifest to
face all of them at once.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:11.300
But, with that being said, you want the end
of the movie to be the climax, the scariest

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.610
part, so I don't think that having a spider
is really the best option.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.770
And this is also something that's touched
on in the book, I forget who it was, but somebody's

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.010
thinking that a spider is something that you
might see crawling around in your kitchen,

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:27.400
something that you experience in real life,
whereas killer clowns are not, so that makes

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.310
it a lot easier for them to face.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:33.699
I would like to see the Spider form come up
at some point during that confrontation in

00:07:33.699 --> 00:07:36.960
Part 2, but I don't think that it should be
the final boss.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:41.080
Another clue towards the possible inclusion
of the spider, again, I've talked about this

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.530
before, but...

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.110
The Dark Tower movie.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:48.900
It may or may not have tie-ins with this IT
movie, I know they're made by different studios,

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.289
but there are a lot of Stephen King references
in The Dark Tower movie, one of which being

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:56.379
when they're at an abandoned amusement park
and they're sitting by the fire talking about

00:07:56.379 --> 00:08:02.190
the monsters that live in this outer realm
that surrounds their central universe.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:06.919
I forget what the exact terms for it are but
you're gonna have to bear with me on that.

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.200
So he draws in the sand.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:13.060
He shows their center universe and he shows
the creatures that are trying to get in from

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:17.590
outside and the creature that's used as an
example is tarantula, which crawls into the

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.850
barrier and comes to where they are.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.160
So if the movies are connected, that could
be some kind of foreshadowing for the fact

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.560
that the spider creature will appear again.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.180
Sammy Saldana, "Do you know if Richie will
die because in the trailer it showed something

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.180
like that?"

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:36.570
In book and in the mini-series Richie does
not die, he is one of the survivors and I

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.620
can't really see them killing him off in this
one.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.710
Like I said, I think the only two major differences
are gonna be the fact that this takes place

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:47.370
in the 80s rather than the 50s and the non-linear
story structure being shifted into a more

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:49.950
linear one just focusing on the kids in Part
1.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.260
In any event, in this first movie I can't
really see any of the kids dying.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.860
We even see in the trailer the scene of the
promise and they all seem to be present for

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:58.860
that.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.490
So I think everybody at least makes it on
to Part 2.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:04.170
Blitzon Benth asks, "Do you think Pennywise
will reveal his true form?"

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:07.209
And there were a lot of questions about this
asking, "Do you think that we'll see the spider?"

00:09:07.209 --> 00:09:09.190
"Do you think we'll see the true form?"

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.330
And in my mind this is just a little bit different
than the question about the spider because

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:18.100
he could be referring to The Deadlights as
Pennywise's true form, not the spider.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:22.820
And of course it's gonna depend how you interpret
it, but I see The Deadlights as the true form

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:28.330
of IT, whereas Pennywise and the spider are
just different manifestations, including some

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.940
of the other ones that I talked about.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.390
So do I think that The Deadlights are gonna
be in this movie?

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:36.220
We haven't really seen any evidence of it
in the trailer, but there is this one shot

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:40.850
of Beverly being lifted up off of the ground,
which could also tie in to phrase, "you'll

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:44.670
float too," and there seems to be some kind
of light shining on her, so I think that could

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:45.950
be the work of The Deadlights.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:49.570
I do think we'll see The Deadlights make a
return in this adaptation.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:52.630
So that just about covers the questions you
guys asked on Twitter.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.920
I'm gonna be seeing this movie as early as
possible and get cooking on hopefully a new

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:00.380
episode of Things You Missed, so be on the
lookout for that.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:05.010
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that death-bell for

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:08.079
notifications and I'll see you in the next
one.

00:10:08.079 --> 00:10:10.320
Assuming we both survive.

